hadiths[200]{hadithnumber,text}:
"801","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith: ""Whoever, as a youth, honors an elderly person because of his age, Allah Almighty will appoint for him someone who will honor him in his old age."""
"802","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever honors an elderly person because of his age, Allah will appoint for him someone who will honor him in his old age."""
"803","It is narrated from Yahya bin Abi Kathir that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the house that is filled with joys is surely filled with admonition and advice, and after every joy, sorrow surely comes."""
"804","Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If a servant is appointed by Allah as a ruler over the people and he does not act with goodwill towards them, Allah will make Paradise forbidden for him."""
"805","Hasan says that Ubaydullah bin Ziyad visited Sayyiduna Ma'qil bin Yasar (may Allah be pleased with him) during the illness in which he passed away. Ma'qil (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Indeed, I am narrating to you a hadith which I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). If I knew that my life would continue, I would not narrate this hadith to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Any servant whom Allah makes a ruler over the people, and he dies on the day of his death while deceiving his people, then Allah makes Paradise forbidden for him."" Imam Muslim has also narrated something similar with his chain, and in it, instead of (ghashsha li ra’iyyatihi) ""deceiving his people,"" the words are (wa huwa ghash) ""and he is a deceiver."""
"806","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Malik al-Dar reports that Ziyad came to visit Abdullah bin Mughaffal (may Allah be pleased with him) during his illness. Abdullah bin Mughaffal (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: O Ziyad! Fear Allah, for the evil of rulers is a destructive thing. Ziyad said to him: You are among the lowest of the companions of Muhammad (peace be upon him). He replied: There was no one lowly among the companions of Muhammad (peace be upon him). O Ziyad! Shall I not tell you something which I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)? He said: Why not (tell me), but do not attribute a lie to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). He said: If (hypothetically) I were to lie about any ordinary person, I would still never lie about the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""Any ruler who spends the night deceiving his people, the fragrance and breeze of Paradise will be forbidden to him, even though its fragrance comes from a distance of seventy years."" The narrator says that Ziyad said to him: Ask me for whatever you wish. He said: I only ask you that you neither benefit me nor harm me; if I fall ill, do not come to visit me, and if I die, do not attend my funeral. The narrator says that only a few nights had passed when he (Abdullah) passed away. Ziyad saw people crowding around his funeral. He said: Who is this? The people said: Abdullah bin Mughaffal. He said: By Allah! If he had not asked me not to attend his funeral, I would certainly have attended it."
"807","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the Muslims, there is no man with a greater reward than a righteous minister who stays with a ruler, obeys him, and commands him to obey Allah, the Exalted."""
"808","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the people, there is no one with greater reward than a righteous minister who stays with a ruler, obeys him, and commands him to obey Allah, the Exalted."""
"809","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every believer has some sin which he commits from time to time; he does not give it up until he leaves this world. And indeed, the believer has been created very forgetful; when he is reminded (to repent), he remembers."""
"810","Sayyiduna Abu Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whenever the sun rises, there are two angels on its two sides who say: O Allah! Grant a quick replacement to the one who spends, and quickly destroy the wealth of the one who withholds.”"
"811","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two ravenous wolves let loose among a flock of sheep do not cause as much harm so quickly as the love of wealth and status does to a Muslim's religion."""
"812","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two ravenous wolves, let loose among a flock of sheep in a strong enclosure, do not cause as much harm quickly as the love of wealth and status does to a Muslim's religion."""
"813","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two ravenous wolves spending the night in a sheepfold do not cause as much harm as the love of wealth and status does to a Muslim's religion."""
"814","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No act of worship to Allah has been performed that is superior to understanding (comprehension) in religion."""
"815","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is nothing greater than maintaining ties of kinship in which Allah is obeyed and its reward is received quickly, and there is no deed greater than rebellion and disobedience in which Allah is disobeyed and its punishment is received quickly."" The chain of narration for the second hadith is as follows: «عن ابيه عن رجل عن يحيىٰ »"
"816","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever opens the door of begging upon himself, Allah opens the door of poverty and neediness upon him, so adopt self-sufficiency."""
"817","Lady Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Charity does not decrease wealth, and when a servant forgives oppression and excess against him, Allah only increases his honor; therefore, you should forgive, Allah will increase your honor. And whoever opens the door of begging upon himself, Allah opens the door of poverty and need upon him."" Al-Tabarani said: Only Qasim bin Yazid Jarami and Zakariya bin Dawud Ash'athi have narrated this hadith from Sufyan Thawri."
"818","Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul, there are three things upon which I can certainly swear: Wealth does not decrease by giving charity, so give charity. And whoever pardons any injustice or oppression seeking the pleasure of Allah, Allah will raise his status on the Day of Resurrection because of it. And whoever opens the door of begging upon himself, Allah opens the door of poverty and need upon him."""
"819","Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “There are three things upon which I swear: Wealth does not decrease by giving charity, so give charity. And when a servant forgives the oppression and excess of someone, Allah increases his honor, so forgive others and Allah will increase your honor. And whoever opens the door of begging upon himself, Allah opens the door of poverty and need upon him. Listen! There is goodness in refraining from begging.” It has been said: This hadith is rare among the narrations of Abu Salamah from his father."
"820","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that a man abused Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was also present. He (the Prophet) was amazed and was smiling. When the man became more insolent, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) replied to one of his remarks. At this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) became angry and stood up. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) got up and went to him and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! He was abusing me while you were present, but when I replied to one of his remarks, you became angry and stood up?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there was an angel with you who was replying to him, but when you replied to him, Satan appeared, so I am not one to sit with Satan."" And the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abu Bakr! These things are true, so learn them: Whoever is wronged and overlooks it, Allah grants him strength and help in return. And whoever opens the door of giving as an act of truthfulness and maintaining family ties, Allah gives him more in return. And whoever opens the door of asking out of greed for abundance, Allah, because of that, increases his scarcity."""
"821","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever opens the door of begging upon himself, Allah opens the door of poverty and neediness upon him. If a person were to take a rope, go to the mountain (or forest), gather a bundle of wood on his back, and then (sell it and) eat from it, this is better for him than going around asking people—whether they give him something or not."""
"822","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever among you opens the door of begging upon himself, Allah will open the door of poverty and need upon him."""
"823","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Each one of you is only awaiting either overwhelming affluence, or impoverishing poverty, or a ruinous illness, or old age that takes away intellect and senses, or sudden, swift death, or the Dajjal (Antichrist). So the Dajjal is the worst hidden thing being awaited, or the Hour (Day of Judgment), for the Hour is a greater calamity and more bitter."""
"824","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Each one of you is only awaiting either overwhelming affluence, or forgetful poverty, or overpowering old age, or a corrupting illness, or sudden, swift death, or the Dajjal (Antichrist)—for he is the worst hidden thing being awaited—or the Hour (Day of Judgment)—for the Hour is a greater calamity and more bitter."""
"825","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whatever fatigue, illness, fever, hardship, or sorrow befalls a believer, even that worry which grieves him, Allah, because of it, forgives his sins."""
"826","Hamzah bin Abdullah says that we set out towards the land of Sham to beg, and when we came to Madinah, Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Are you going to Sham to beg? Whereas I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""A servant keeps begging until he meets Allah (on the Day of Resurrection he will meet Allah) in such a state that there will not be a piece of flesh on his face."" Imam Muslim has also narrated this with his chain in a marfu' form: One of you keeps begging until he meets Allah (on the Day of Resurrection he will meet Him) in such a state that there will not be a piece of flesh on his face."
"827","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer is not bitten from the same hole twice."""
"828","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith. Imam Muslim has narrated it with his chain from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) in marfu‘ form: A believer is not bitten from the same hole twice."
"829","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard Sayyiduna Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever does not thank people, does not thank Allah either."""
"830","Sayyiduna Ash'ath bin Qais (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not thank people, does not thank Allah either."""
"831","Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say... then he narrated this hadith: ""Supplication alone can avert destiny, and righteousness alone can prolong life."""
"832","Sayyiduna Salman al-Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Only righteousness can prolong life, and only supplication can avert destiny."""
"833","Sayyiduna Salman al-Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Only righteousness can prolong life, and only supplication can avert destiny."""
"834","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Forbearance comes only after stumbling, and wisdom and understanding are attained only through experience.” The narrator Sabuni stated in his narration as follows: «أخبرنا عبد الله بن وهب أخبرني عمرو بن الحارث»"
"835","Abu al-Abbas bin Qutaybah Asqalani says: Yazid bin Muhib Ramli narrated to us with his chain of transmission that indeed Abu al-Samh Darraj narrated this hadith and he agreed with it until the end of the text. Abu al-Abbas bin Qutaybah said: Some of my companions said to me: Ahmad bin Hanbal said to me (Muhib bin Yazid): What did you write in the land of al-Sham? I said to him: I wrote this hadith. So he said: If you had written nothing else there except this, even then your journey would not have been wasted."
"836","Harith reports that Ali (peace be upon him) asked his son Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) about certain things and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""There is no poverty greater than ignorance, no wealth that returns more than intellect, no loneliness more terrifying than self-admiration, no demonstration stronger than consultation, no wisdom like planning, no beauty like good character, no piety like refraining from sin, no worship like contemplation, and no faith like patience and modesty."""
"837","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that indeed he (peace be upon him) said: ""O Abu Dharr! There is no wisdom like planning, no piety like refraining from sin, and no nobility like good character."""
"838","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""There is no poverty greater than ignorance, no wealth that returns more than intellect, no piety like refraining from sin, and no worship like contemplation."""
"839","Muhammad bin Munkadir narrates from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""After reaching puberty, there is no (status of) orphanhood."""
"840","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no (new) covenant or pact in Islam like that of the Age of Ignorance."""
"841","Sayyiduna Qais bin Asim (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no (new) covenant or pact in Islam (like those of the Age of Ignorance), and whatever was established in the Age of Ignorance, hold firmly to it."""
"842","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no celibacy in Islam."" Abu Ja'far Tahawi said: We have not found in this chapter any hadith with a connected chain to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) other than this hadith."
"843","Ikrimah reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""There is no celibacy in Islam."""
"844","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After the conquest (of Makkah), there is no (obligatory) migration, but jihad and intention remain. And when you are called to go out for jihad, then set out (without hesitation)."""
"845","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that when this verse was revealed: « إذَا جَاءَ نَصْرُ اللَّهِ وَالْفَتْحُ » (An-Nasr: 1), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recited it until he completed (reciting) it, then said: ""I am on one side and my Companions are also on one side (while all the rest of the people are on the other side). After the conquest, there is no migration."""
"846","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no migration after the conquest, but jihad and intention remain, and when you are called to go out for jihad, then go forth."""
"847","Mansur has also narrated it in the same manner with his chain of transmission."
"848","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""He who has no trustworthiness has no faith, and he who does not keep his promise has no religion."""
"849","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) addressed us, he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever has no trustworthiness has no faith, and whoever has no covenant has no religion."""
"850","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) addressed us, he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has no trustworthiness, has no faith."""
"851","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Blood money is only due to a wound caused by a glance or a sting."""
"852","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible to sever relations for more than three days."""
"853","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No major sin remains with seeking forgiveness, and no minor sin remains with persistence."""
"854","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no grief except the grief of debt, and there is no pain except the pain of the eye."" In the narration of Harithi, Imam Tabarani said: Only Ibn Abi Dhi’b narrates it from Muhammad bin Munkadir, and Sahl bin Qareen is unique in narrating it from him."
"855","It is narrated from Hasan that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""There is no poverty for the one who recites the Qur'an, and without it, there is no richness for him."""
"856","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that a woman from Banu Khathma satirized the Prophet (peace be upon him). When the Prophet (peace be upon him) was informed of this, he became very angry and said: ""Who will take revenge on my behalf from her?"" Then a man from that woman's tribe said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I will (do it)."" That woman used to sell dates. That man came to her (and said): ""Are there any better dates than these?"" She entered the house (to bring better dates), and the man entered right after her. He looked around and saw nothing except a dining table, so he picked it up and struck her on the head with it, causing her brains to come out. Then he came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I have taken care of her on your behalf."" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Not even the heads of two goats will clash over her."" Thus, the Prophet (peace be upon him) made this statement proverbial."
"857","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that a woman from Banu Khathma satirized the Prophet (peace be upon him). When this was reported to him, he became very angry and said: ""Who will take revenge on my behalf from her?"" A man from her tribe said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I will take revenge on your behalf."" That woman used to sell dates. The narrator says that the man came to her and said: ""Do you have dates?"" She said: ""Yes."" She showed him the dates, so the man said: ""I want better dates than these."" She entered the house (to bring better dates), and the man entered after her. He looked around and saw nothing except a dining table, so he picked it up and struck her on the head with it until her brain came out. Then he came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I have sufficed you regarding her."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) then said: ""Not even the heads of two goats will clash over this."" Thus, the Prophet (peace be upon him) made this statement proverbial."
"858","Abdullah bin Harith bin Fazl narrates from his father, who said: Asma bint Marwan was from Banu Umayyah bin Zaid, and Yazid bin Zaid bin Hisn Khatmi was her husband. She used to incite (people) against the Muslims, harass them, and recite insulting poetry. Umair bin Adi made a vow that if Allah the Exalted brought His Messenger (peace be upon him) back safely from the Battle of Badr, then he (Umair) would surely kill this woman. The narrator says that (when the Prophet returned from the Battle of Badr) Umair, fulfilling his vow, attacked her in the darkness of the night and put her to death. He then met the Prophet (peace be upon him) and performed the morning prayer with him. The Prophet (peace be upon him) kept looking at him attentively, and when he got up to go to his house, he said to Umair bin Adi: ""Did you kill Asma?"" He said: Yes. (Umair says) I said: O Messenger of Allah! Is there anything (blood money or sin, etc.) upon me for her killing? Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Not even two goats will butt heads over her."" This phrase (idiom) was heard for the first time from the pure tongue of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)."
"859","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Caution cannot save from destiny, and supplication is beneficial for calamity that has already descended and that which has not yet descended. Indeed, when calamity descends, supplication confronts it, and they wrestle with each other until the Day of Resurrection."""
"860","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Caution cannot save from destiny, and if anything could prevent sustenance, it would be weeping and wailing that could prevent it, and indeed supplication benefits against calamity."" Indeed, Allah has said in His Book: «سوائے قوم یونس کے کہ جب وہ ایمان لائے تو ہم نے رسوائی کا عذاب ان سے دور کر دیا» ""(That is), when they supplicated."" These are the words of the narrator Yaqub bin Ishaq."
"861","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Caution cannot save from destiny, and supplication is beneficial for what has been decreed, and indeed supplication confronts calamity, and they wrestle with each other until the Day of Resurrection."""
"862","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Caution cannot save from destiny, but supplication is beneficial for calamity that has already descended and that which has not yet descended. Therefore, O servants of Allah! Hold fast to supplication."""
"863","Sayyiduna Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer does not kill by deception."""
"864","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That nation will never prosper which makes a woman its ruler."""
"865","Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said . . . . . . and he narrated this hadith."
"866","Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not befitting for a believer to humiliate himself."""
"867","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not befitting for a believer to humiliate himself."" The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) asked: O Messenger of Allah! How can he humiliate himself? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He exposes himself to trials which he cannot bear."""
"868","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said . . . . . . and he narrated this hadith. And with another chain of narration, it is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""It does not befit a truthful person to be greatly given to cursing."" Imam Muslim has also narrated it with his chain, and in it (instead of ""al-siddiq"") there is ""li-siddiq"" with a ""lam."""
"869","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""It is not possible for a two-faced person to be trustworthy with Allah."""
"870","Zuhri reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Expressing helplessness and incapacity is appropriate only before parents and a just ruler.”"
"871","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Doing good is appropriate only for a person of family or religiousness, just as asceticism is a fine trait only in a human being."""
"872","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Doing good is appropriate only with a person of family or a religious person."""
"873","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""There is no obedience to the creation in disobedience to the Creator."" (Its chain) in the original is Hammad from Ibn ‘Awn from Muhammad bin Sirin, while in ""Al-Fawa’id"" it is Hammad from Ibn Sirin."
"874","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul, a person cannot enter Paradise if his neighbor is not safe from his harm."""
"875","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that indeed he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That person will not enter Paradise whose neighbor is not safe from his harm."" Imam Muslim has also narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) with his chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That person will not enter Paradise whose neighbor is not safe from his harm."""
"876","Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""The tale-bearer will not enter Paradise."""
"877","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not lawful for any Muslim to frighten another Muslim."""
"878","Abdur Rahman bin Abi Laila narrates that the companions of Muhammad (peace be upon him) told us that indeed they were traveling with the Prophet (peace be upon him) at night. One of them fell asleep, so a person took his rope and went towards him and grabbed him, so he got scared. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a Muslim to frighten another Muslim."""
"879","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said . . . . . and he narrated this hadith."
"880","Muhammad bin Sa’d narrates from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: “It is not lawful for a person to sever relations with his brother for more than three days.”"
"881","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""It is not lawful for any Muslim to sever relations with his brother for more than three days; when they meet, each turns away from the other, and the better of the two is the one who initiates the greeting of peace (salam)."""
"882","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""It is not lawful for a believer to sever relations with his brother for more than three days."""
"883","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that it is not permissible for any Muslim to sever relations with his brother for more than three days."
"884","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not lawful for a wealthy person to take charity, nor for a strong and healthy person."""
"885","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not lawful for a wealthy person to take charity, nor for a strong and healthy person."""
"886","Abu al-Bakhtari says that the person who heard from the Prophet (peace be upon him) narrated to me that the Prophet (peace be upon him) was saying: ""People will never be destroyed until their disobedience becomes excessive or they are left with no excuse."""
"887","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “A person’s faith cannot be correct until his heart is correct, and his heart cannot be correct until his tongue is correct.”"
"888","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul, a servant cannot be a believer until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."""
"889","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""A servant cannot be a believer until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."""
"890","Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""A servant cannot attain the reality of faith until he is certain that whatever has reached him could not have missed him, and whatever has missed him could not have reached him (in any way)."""
"891","Sayyiduna Abu Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “A servant cannot perfect the reality of faith until he is certain that whatever has reached him could not have missed him, and whatever has missed him could not have reached him (in any way).”"
"892","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ammar bin Yasir (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A servant cannot perfect his faith until he possesses three qualities: spending in times of hardship, being just with his own self, and spreading the greeting of peace widely."""
"893","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you can perfect the reality of faith until he controls his tongue."""
"894","Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Allah does not show mercy to the one who does not show mercy to people."""
"895","Abayah bin Rifaa says that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) received news that Saad (may Allah be pleased with him) had built a palace, so he sent a message to him saying: ""Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'A believer does not fill his stomach while his neighbor (remains hungry) without food.'"""
"896","Abayah bin Rifaa says that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) received news that Saad (may Allah be pleased with him) had built a palace, so he sent a message to him: ""Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say this?"" And he narrated this hadith."
"897","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A scholar is never satiated with knowledge until his end is Paradise."""
"898","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “(The affairs of) the world will only become more severe, the world will continue to decline, miserliness will only increase among people, the Hour will be established upon the worst of people, and ‘Isa ibn Maryam (peace be upon him) is indeed the Mahdi.”"
"899","This hadith is also narrated through another chain from Muhammad bin Khalid Jundi with his chain in the same manner."
"900","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said . . . . . . and he narrated this hadith."
"901","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “(The affairs of the world) will only become more severe, wealth will only increase, and the Hour will be established upon the worst of Allah’s creation.”"
"902","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""The Hour will be established only upon the worst of people."""
"903","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says: ""Every era that comes upon you will be worse than the one before it."" We heard this from your Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"904","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not come until men become few and women become many."""
"905","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever conceals the faults of a servant in this world, Allah will conceal his faults on the Day of Resurrection."""
"906","This hadith is also narrated through another chain from Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Jami' with his chain in the same manner."
"907","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “A person is upon the religion of his friend, and there is no good in the company of one who does not wish good for you in the same way as you wish for him.”"
"908","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If a servant loses his two beloved things (his eyes), then remains patient and hopes for reward, he will enter Paradise."""
"909","Sayyiduna Atiyyah Sa'di (may Allah be pleased with him), who attained the honor of being a Companion, reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A servant cannot reach the rank of the pious until he leaves even those things in which there is no harm, in order to avoid doubtful matters."""
"910","Sayyiduna Atiyyah Sa'di (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""A servant cannot reach the rank of the pious until he leaves even those things in which there is no harm, in order to avoid doubtful matters."""
"911","Sayyiduna Atiyyah Sa'di, may Allah be pleased with him, who is among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A servant cannot reach the rank of the pious until he abandons even those things in which there is no harm, in order to avoid doubtful matters."""
"912","It is also narrated in a similar way from Sayyiduna Atiyyah Sa'di (may Allah be pleased with him) through another chain, and in it is: ""To avoid doubtful matters."""
"913","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""A group from my Ummah will always remain dominant upon the truth until Allah's decision comes."""
"914","Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “A group from my Ummah will always remain dominant upon the truth; those who oppose them will not be able to harm them in any way, until Allah’s decision comes.”"
"915","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""A servant's soul remains suspended because of his debt until it is paid off on his behalf."""
"916","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""As long as a servant waits for the prayer, he remains in the state of prayer."""
"917","Sayyiduna Wathilah bin Asqa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Do not express joy at your brother’s hardship, lest Allah grants him well-being and puts you to trial.”"
"918","Sayyiduna Wathilah bin Asqa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say . . . . . . and he narrated this hadith."
"919","Sayyiduna Wathilah bin Asqa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Do not express joy over your brother’s distress, lest Allah has mercy on him and puts you to trial.”"
"920","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not revile time, for Allah is (the Creator of) time."""
"921","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: The son of Adam hurts Me; he abuses time, whereas I am time (i.e., the Creator of time). All authority is in My hand; I am the One Who alternates the night and the day."""
"922","Zaid bin Aslam narrates from his father that he set out towards the land of Shaam with Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him). He says: Then I heard Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah bin Jarrah (may Allah be pleased with him) saying that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Do not abuse the ruler, for he is Allah's shade on His earth."""
"923","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Do not revile the dead, for they have already attained what they sent forth."""
"924","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said . . . . . . and she narrated this hadith."
"925","Sayyiduna Mughirah bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Do not revile the dead, for by doing so you will harm the living.”"
"926","It is narrated from Hasan that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A man should not return his brother's gift, and if he finds (something with him), then he must surely give a good recompense."""
"927","Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not wipe your hand on the garment of a person whom you have not clothed."""
"928","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade that a person should wipe his hand on the garment of someone whom he has not clothed."
"929","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: ""Do not turn away a beggar, even if it is with only a piece of date."""
"930","Amr bin Mu'adh Ansari narrates from his grandmother Sayyida Hawwa (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Do not turn away a beggar (empty-handed), even if it is (by giving) a hoof."""
"931","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said . . . . . . and he narrated this hadith."
"932","It is narrated from Matlub bin Khatab that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Do not turn away a beggar (empty-handed), even if it is only a burnt house."""
"933","Sayyiduna Abu Barzah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not backbite the Muslims, nor seek out their faults."""
"934","Ibn Jabir says that I heard an elder in Beirut whose kunya was Abu ‘Amr. I am certain that he narrated a hadith to me from Umm Darda’ that a man called Harmalah came to the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him), pointed to his tongue and said: “Iman is here,” and pointed to his heart and said: “Nifaq is here.” (Then he said:) “I remember Allah very little.” The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: “O Allah! Make his tongue one that remembers (You) and his heart one that is grateful . . . . . .” And he narrated a long hadith in which it was also mentioned: “Never disclose anyone’s fault.”"
"935","Sayyiduna Abu Jari Hajimi (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! We are people of the desert, teach us a deed, perhaps through it Allah Almighty will benefit us."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Never consider any act of goodness to be insignificant."""
"936","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not make a promise to your brother which you will break."""
"937","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should ever wish for death because of any hardship that has befallen him."""
"938","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say, three days before his passing: “Beware! Let none of you die except while he has good expectations of Allah.”"
"939","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Do not envy one another, and do not artificially raise prices without the intention of buying, and do not harbor malice against one another, and do not turn your backs on one another. O servants of Allah! Become brothers to one another."""
"940","Makhul reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Do not be fault-finders, nor praisers, nor those who taunt, nor those who show weakness in deeds."""
"941","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Bahili رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم said: ""Do not be amazed at the deeds of any doer until you see what his end is upon."""
"942","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not consider anyone's Islam to be good until you know how deep his understanding is."""
"943","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not consider anyone's Islam to be good until you know how much understanding he possesses."""
"944","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: ""Do not make me like the cup of a rider (traveler)."" The companions asked: What is the cup of a rider? He said: ""Indeed, a traveler carries his belongings on his mount, and if water remains in his cup, he pours it back into his water-skin."" He said: ""Place me at the beginning, the middle, and the end (in all three places) of your speech."""
"945","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon to us, and in his sermon he said: ""The fear of people should never prevent any of you from speaking the truth when he knows it."""
"946","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) addressed the people at the place of Jabiyah and said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood in this manner and he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No man should be alone with a woman, for the third among them is the devil."""
"947","Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Never seek to please anyone by incurring Allah's displeasure; never praise anyone for what Allah has bestowed upon you; and never blame anyone for what Allah has not given you, because no one's greed can bring Allah's provision to you, nor can anyone's ill will prevent it from reaching you."" In the chain of narration, Khalid bin Najeeh is mentioned in this way, although in reality this hadith is narrated through the chain of Khalid bin Yazid al-‘Umari from Sufyan al-Thawri."
"948","Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Samurah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم said to me: ""Do not ask for leadership, because if it is given to you without your asking, you will be helped in it, and if it is given to you because of your asking, you will be left to it (on your own)."""
"949","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""The Hour will not be established until children become a cause of anger and rage, rain becomes a cause of intense heat, vile people become widespread, the noble become angry, the young glare at the elders, and the lowly glare at the noble."""
"950","Saeed bin Musayyib narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A person is never ruined after consultation."""
"951","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A people with an oppressive and wicked populace will never be destroyed as long as their rulers are rightly guided and guided, and even if the populace is rightly guided and guided but the rulers are oppressive and wicked, they will never be destroyed."""
"952","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! Please tell me a hadith and keep it brief so that I can remember it. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray as if you are bidding farewell (to this world), as if you will not pray again after this. And despair of what people possess, you will live a life of contentment. And avoid that which you would later need to apologize for."""
"953","Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Beware of excessive praise, for it is (like) slaughter."""
"954","Sayyiduna Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah intends good for someone, He grants him understanding of the religion."" He (peace be upon him) also said: ""Beware of excessive praise, for it is (like) slaughtering."""
"955","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Aisha! Beware even of sins that are considered minor, for there is also a demander from Allah for them."""
"956","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Avoid seeking people's opinions, for it exposes faults and buries beauty."""
"957","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Beware of the greenery that grows in filthy places."" It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is meant by the greenery that grows in filthy places? He said: ""A beautiful woman who has been raised in a bad environment."""
"958","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Avoid (unnecessary) taking of loans, for it is a cause of grief at night and humiliation during the day."""
"959","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the greatest falsehood."""
"960","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of the supplication of the oppressed, even if he is a disbeliever, for there is no barrier between it and Allah."""
"961","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, some speech is magic, some poetry is wisdom, some statements are burdens, and some knowledge is ignorance."""
"962","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, some poetry contains wisdom, and indeed, some speech is magic."""
"963","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that two men came from the east and delivered a sermon; the people liked their speech very much. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, some speech is magic."" Or: ""Indeed, some eloquence is magic."""
"964","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, some poetry contains wisdom."""
"965","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, some poetry contains wisdom."""
"966","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) in a marfu‘ form that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, some poetry contains wisdom, and indeed, some speech is magic.”"
"967","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, my Ummah is an Ummah upon whom mercy has been bestowed (that is, it has been granted special mercy)."""
"968","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Indeed, this Ummah is an Ummah upon whom mercy has been bestowed; there is no punishment for it in the Hereafter. Its punishment has been made in this world in the form of killing, tribulations, and earthquakes."""
"969","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My Ummah is an Ummah upon whom mercy has been bestowed; there is no punishment for it in the Hereafter. Its punishment is only in this world in the form of earthquakes and killings."""
"970","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah says: When I entered Bukhara, my first gathering was with the ruler Isma'il bin Ahmad among a group of scholars. There, several hadiths were mentioned. The ruler Isma'il narrated this hadith: ""My ummah is an ummah granted mercy . . . . . ."" etc., with this chain: «حدثنا ابي حدثنا يزيد بن هارون عن حميد عن انس قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم . . . . . .» I said: May Allah support the ruler, this hadith has neither been narrated by Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), nor by Humaid, nor by Yazid bin Harun. The ruler Isma'il became silent, then began to ask: How is that? I replied: This hadith is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him), and it is based upon him. When the gathering dispersed, Abu Ali Salih bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi said to me: Abu Bakr! May Allah reward you with goodness, this ruler has mentioned this chain to us several times, but none of us had the courage to refute it. Abu 'Abdullah said: In fact, the purpose of the ruler Isma'il bin Ahmad was to narrate this hadith with this chain: «يزيد بن هارون عن المسعودي عن سعيد بن ابي بردة بن ابي موسى عن ابيه عن جده . . . . . .» I say: The hadith of Muhammad bin Bakr bin Fadl al-Faqih, which we have narrated, its chain ends with Humaid from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), and this is the hadith which our shaykh Muhammad 'Abd al-Ghani has extracted in this book in which he has collected the authentic narrations of Muhammad bin Bakr according to the conditions of Bukhari and Muslim, while the hadith of Mas'udi, we have narrated it with the chain of al-Bazzar."
"971","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said . . . . . . and she narrated a hadith in which it was also mentioned: ""Maintaining friendship is part of faith."""
"972","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that an old woman used to come to the Prophet (peace be upon him). He would be pleased with her and honor her. I said: ""May my parents be sacrificed for you, the way you treat this old woman, you do not treat anyone else like this."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this woman used to come to Khadijah. Do you not know that maintaining friendship is part of faith?"""
"973","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Indeed, having good expectations is part of good worship."""
"974","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, having good expectations is part of good worship."""
"975","Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Indeed, the scholars are the heirs of the prophets."""
"976","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Indeed, the religion is easy, and whoever makes the religion too hard upon himself, it will overpower him. So remain steadfast, be moderate, and seek help (in worship) in the morning, evening, and a part of the night."""
"977","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said . . . . . . and he narrated a hadith in which it was also stated: ""Indeed, the religion of Allah is straight and easy."""
"978","Abu Salamah narrates from his father that indeed the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the quickest reward for any good deed is for maintaining the ties of kinship."""
"979","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said . . . . . . and he narrated a hadith in which it was also mentioned: ""Indeed, wisdom increases the nobility of a noble person..."""
"980","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""Indeed, the one who makes a lawful thing unlawful is just like the one who makes an unlawful thing lawful."""
"981","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever makes a lawful thing unlawful is just like the one who makes an unlawful thing lawful."""
"982","Sayyiduna Buraidah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Indeed, the lineage of the people of this world is wealth."""
"983","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said in a lengthy hadith: ""Indeed, the one who has a right has the right to speak."""
"984","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (the Prophet) took a camel of a certain age from someone. Its owner came to you to demand it back, so the Companions spoke harshly to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the owner of a right has the right to speak."" Then you gave him a better camel than the one of his age and fulfilled his right, and said: ""The best among you is the one who is best in repayment."""
"985","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed he fell ill, so some of his (religious) brothers came to visit him. He said to his maidservant: Maid! Quickly bring something for our brothers, even if it is just a piece of bread, because I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Indeed, high moral character is among the deeds of the people of Paradise."""
"986","Sayyiduna Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the best beauty is the beauty of character."" In the chain of narration, the first Hasan refers to Hasan ibn Sahl, the second to Ibn Dinar, the third to Basri, and the fourth to Sayyiduna Hasan ibn Ali (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"987","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Rafi’ (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, the freed slave of a people is counted among them.”"
"988","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the freed slave of a people is counted among them."""
"989","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the majority of the people of Paradise will be simple-hearted people."""
"990","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, the majority of the people of Paradise will be simple-hearted people."""
"991","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the inhabitants of Paradise, women are very few."""
"992","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, help comes to a servant in proportion to his responsibility, and indeed, patience comes to a servant in proportion to his calamity.”"
"993","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the greatest act of goodness is that a person maintains ties with his father's friends."""
"994","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the greatest act of goodness is that a person treats his father's friends well after his father's death."" Muslim ibn Hajjaj has also narrated with his chain: ""Indeed, the greatest act of goodness is that a person maintains ties with his father's friends after his father's death."""
"995","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the Shay..."
"996","Sayyiduna Ash'ath bin Qais (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the people, the most grateful to Allah is the one who is most grateful to the people."""
"997","Sayyiduna Ash'ath bin Qais (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the most grateful to Allah among the people is the one who is most grateful to the people."""
"998","Sayyiduna Ash'ath bin Qais (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the most grateful to Allah among the people is the one who is most grateful to the people."""
"999","It is narrated from Mutarrif that indeed one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, related to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, the acquisition of this wealth is a trial, and withholding it is also a trial."""
"1000","Sayyiduna Abu Burdah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I was sitting with Ubaydullah bin Ziyad when the heads of the Khawarij were being brought to him one after another. Whenever a head was brought to him, I would say: For Hell. He says that then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Yazid Hatmi (may Allah be pleased with him) spoke up: O nephew! Do you not know that indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Indeed, the punishment of this Ummah has been placed in its world."""
